                    User's Manual for the NoAnsi utility.


1. Introduction

   Well, this util was created due to the irritating fact that with
   AmiExpress you always have to run the Utils twice, once for Ansi
   and once for NO Ansi. This seemed pretty wastfull to me, so I
   started thinking if you couldn't solve this problem somehow. And,
   voila! NoAnsi is here.

   2. How to get started

   The usage if the NoAnsi util looks like this:

   NoAnsi [InputFile] [Output File]

   The input file is the textfile containing Ansi graphics, and the
   outputfile is where you want the resultfile, containing NO Ansi,
   to go. (The Output file may, as always, be specified to a '*' to
   bring the output onto the current CLI/Shell window). I don't
   really think there's any need for an example about this util.
   It work pretty much like the regular CLI-copy command anyway.


3. Hints?

   Nah... What hints can there be about a sort of a copy-command?
   Like I said before; run NoAnsi instead of that extra time you
   run your util.

4. Versions?

   Nah... Nothing here either. I mean, it's just not big enough.

